      "content": "Okay, so you're saying it's a high probability they are lying. But what about the defense's argument that these aren't \"lies\" but just \"differing interpretations of the same events\"? They claim the documents are being taken out of context to manufacture these contradictions. \n\nIf you're applying that same logic to both sides, why does it feel like the \"interpretation\" excuse is being used as a shield for the witness, while the opposition's claims are dismissed as \"verifiable facts\"? Can you look at the specific phrasing the defense uses to justify the contradictions and tell me if that's a legitimate legal defense or just a way to obfuscate the truth?",
